+# Review: `layer(base, over)`
+
+Each item of `docs/REVIEW-CHECKLIST.md`, with the file and line that satisfies it.
+
+1. **Met.** `src/layer.mjs:18` exports `layer`.
+2. **Met.** `src/layer.mjs:26-41` layers plain objects key by key and lets any
+   other value in `over` replace the one in `base`. Tests in
+   `tests/layer.test.mjs`: the checklist example at line 19; keys only one
+   layer has at 23; any depth at 30; an array replacing, whole, at 38; a number
+   at 46; a string at 52; a boolean at 58; `null` at 64.
+3. **Met.** `src/layer.mjs:19-20`, using `isPlainObject` at `src/layer.mjs:3-7`.
+   One test per case and per argument in `tests/layer.test.mjs`: an array at 82
+   and 86; `null` at 90 and 94; a string at 98 and 102; a number at 106 and
+   110; a `Date` at 114 and 118; an argument left out at 122.
+4. **Met.** `layer` only ever writes to objects it made itself: `lay` starts
+   from `{}` (`src/layer.mjs:22`, `:34`, `:45`), arrays are copied item by item
+   (`:49`) and a `Date` is copied (`:53`). Tests: neither argument changes, and
+   frozen arguments are accepted, at `tests/layer.test.mjs:136`; no object or
+   array reachable from the result is one reachable from `base` or `over`, and
+   changing the result changes neither, at `:150`; one object given in several
+   places is copied each time at `:176`.
+5. **Met.** `src/layer.mjs:30` skips the three keys wherever an object is
+   copied, and every object in the result is created by `{}`
+   (`src/layer.mjs:22`, `:34`, `:45`). Tests: the keys at the top level, nested,
+   and inside arrays, from both arguments, at `tests/layer.test.mjs:211`;
+   ordinary prototypes, also for layers that had none, at `:243`.
+6. **Met.** `CHANGELOG.md:5`.
+7. **Met.** `npm test` exits 0: 33 tests, 33 pass, 0 skipped, 0 todo.
+8. **Met.** Changed: `src/layer.mjs`, `tests/layer.test.mjs`, `CHANGELOG.md`,
+   and this record. `README.md` is therefore not updated and does not mention
+   `layer` yet.
+
+## Decisions the checklist leaves open
+
+- A key given as `undefined` in `over` counts as given: it replaces the value
+  in `base` (`tests/layer.test.mjs:76`).
+- An object without a prototype (`Object.create(null)`) counts as a plain
+  object, as an argument and as a value; the result holds an ordinary object in
+  its place.
+- A `Date` value is copied. Any other value that is not plain data (a
+  function, a `Map`, a class instance) cannot be copied faithfully and sharing
+  it would break item 4, so `layer` throws a `TypeError`
+  (`src/layer.mjs:54`, `tests/layer.test.mjs:193`).
+- Settings that contain themselves throw a `TypeError`
+  (`src/layer.mjs:27`, `:47`, `tests/layer.test.mjs:201`).
diff --git a/settingskit/src/layer.mjs b/settingskit/src/layer.mjs
